  "body": "### Summary\nAs the author of LOT-140, I want the MP list around a reply in an **older** unread conversation and in a group conversation, so that reply detection does not rest on a thread that was already row 1.\n\n### Scope\n`R336`-`R338` (#567) show a thread that was created last, so it stayed row 1. They cannot show what a reply does to a row further down. Capture, on the two kit accounts:\n1. An unread conversation that is not row 1 of the MP list: list before and after one reply. Does the row move? (The rows of `R336` are in descending last-post order.)\n2. The same on a group conversation.\n3. A reply by the account that did not create the conversation, and the lists read as that creator.\n\nHFR allows one new MP per account per 60 minutes (`W11x`). These are MP writes between the kit accounts, so the batch needs the operator's go first (LOT-001 checklist).\n\n### Sources\n`docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` §6c \"LOT-140 — MP reply in an unread conversation\", `MANIFEST.md` run 12, `R13` of the capture checklist.\n\n### Wanted by\nLOT-140 (#230).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\nAnonymized list pages and write answers committed, manifest and protocol entry updated, the *pending capture* marks removed.\n",
