   "body": "### Capture result (scope 2, group)\n\nPR #748 holds `W610e`-`W610g` and `R610e`-`R610h`; it merges after #739. The operator gave the go on 2026-11-10, and the two writes that reach the other members were sent by the main session.\n\n- **What HFR does:** a four-member group row behaves like a one-to-one row. A reply by a member who is not the owner lifts it above newer rows by last-post order, and turns it \"Nouveau message\" with the reply count up, in the creator's list. In the replier's own list it is row 1 and also reads \"Nouveau message\". In the creator's view, the `[non lu]` span then names the replier too.\n- **What this changes:** HFR-PROTOCOL §6c LOT-140 (group bullet; no pending mark left). No merged code changes.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
